/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 69 0 R
/E (This report examines the Business Responsibility and Sustainability Reports \(BRSR\) of the chemical industry. Considering the company performance by market capitalization ranking and availability of reports, choose Tata Chemicals Limited \(TCL\), Gujarat Fluorochemicals Limited \(GFL\), and Navin Fluorine International Limited \(NFIL\) for three financial years. TCL operates as a top 1000 listed corporation marked by the Securities and Exchange Board of India, as a diversified, multinational with reporting across geographical locations. GFL is a Gujarat based fluorochemical manufacturer reporting on a standalone basis, while NFIL is a leading fluorochemical and Contract Development and Manufacturing Organisation among international market players with high export background. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
91 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 69 0 R
/E (For the analysis, parts of two sections and principles related to the adherence to national guidelines for responsible business conduct, environment sustainability and human rights and compliance systems and other indicators as metrics are considered. Among the three, TCL stands at the top of the reporting in terms of scale and data depth, while NFIL follows the alignment towards global sustainability certifications. GFL complies with regulatory disclosure norms but provides relatively lean narrative depth.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
